# oracle/patches/0010-oracle-text-decision-log.patch  [P6.15]
#
# THE TEXT ORACLE. Adds a decision log -- glyph draws and window restores, in call order -- and
# a bounded text sweep that opens and closes every logic message so the log has something to
# record. Before this there was NO oracle for text at all: every text opcode is a declared no-op
# on both legs and oracle/dumps/ held nothing for text, so a 6809 text renderer could not have
# been gated against anything [P6.14].
#
# IT LOGS CALLS, NOT PIXELS. oracleDumpScreens (patch 0001) records why the display path is not
# dumped: "it is a rendering of these buffers, and diffing against a rendering would put
# ScummVM's upscaler inside our baseline." That argument transfers to text even though the
# display screen is where text primarily lives -- a 320x200 dump would carry the upscaler, the
# font file and translateFontPosToDisplayScreen into the comparison.
#
# NO GAME TEXT IN THE ARTIFACT. The character code is NOT logged; position, colours and an
# order-sensitive rolling checksum are. CLAUDE.md 2P: counts and hashes only. The gate loses
# nothing -- the reference is handed the same resources, so the checksum proves both sides laid
# out the same string while the artifact stays free of the script.
#
# *** THIS DIFF IS CUMULATIVE FOR THE FOUR FILES IT TOUCHES, NOT INCREMENTAL. ***
# The build tree carries patches 0001-0009 as UNCOMMITTED changes against the pin, so `git diff`
# on agi.cpp / graphics.cpp / graphics.h / text.cpp emits their hunks as well as this task's.
# Applying 0001-0009 and then this file to a clean pin would conflict. Applying THIS file alone
# to a clean pin gives the correct final state for these four files and nothing for the others.
# Splitting it into a true increment needs the series committed rather than stacked in a dirty
# tree, which is a change to how the whole series is kept -- recorded as a follow-up rather than
# done in passing. This header is here so nobody discovers the shape by applying it.
#
